<!--
  Shared admin AREA filter.

  Rendered INSIDE each view's own filter <form>, so the control sits beside
  Date / Shift / Branch instead of existing only as the global banner above the content.

  AREAS ONLY. A commissary is not an area, and listing commissaries in an "area"
  dropdown made them look like areas. Commissary filtering lives on the commissary
  view, which has its own commissary selector.

  It binds to the existing ?scope= parameter, which AdminAreaScope already validates and
  persists per actor, so this adds NO second source of truth and NO per-view SQL.

  The select is wrapped in an admin_view_scope conditional because that context key is only
  injected for role=admin; supervisors and production users get no control and no error. That
  guard is written as a tag below; do NOT spell the tag out in this comment - the DiSyL linter
  counts a tag written in prose as a real opening tag and fails the file for a mismatch.
-->
{if admin_view_scope}
<!-- The visible label is load-bearing, not decoration. Every sibling control in these filter bars is
     <div class="form-group"><label class="form-label">...</label><control>, and the bar centres its
     flex items. Without the label this control measured 39px tall against 66px for its siblings, so
     centring pushed it ~14px BELOW them (measured on Overview: top 305 vs 284/289). Adding the label
     gives it the same box, which is what puts it on the same line as From/To/Branch. -->
<label class="form-label" for="admin-scope-filter">Area</label>
<select class="form-input" id="admin-scope-filter" name="scope"
        onchange="var h=location.href.replace(/[?&]scope=[^&]*/,'').replace(/[?&]$/,'');location.assign(h+(h.indexOf('?')<0?'?':'&')+'scope='+encodeURIComponent(this.value))">
    <option value="ALL" {if admin_view_scope.value == 'ALL'}selected{/if}>All areas</option>
    {foreach admin_view_scope.areas as scope_area}
    <option value="AREA:{scope_area.id}" {if scope_area.selected}selected{/if}>{scope_area.name}</option>
    {/foreach}
</select>
{/if}
